          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "अंग्रेज़ — aṅgrez — \"an English person\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "अंग्रेज़ दो सौ साल तक इस देश में रहे। aṅgrez do sau sāl tak is deś meṁ rahe. The English stayed in this country for two hundred years."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine or feminine, by the person meant."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "अंग्रेज़ (aṅgrez) is usually traced to Portuguese inglês, \"English\", through Persian angrez. अंग्रेज़ी, the English language, is built on it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
